cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "N-PDF Fit: Unbinned Maximum-Likelihood and MCMC Fitting Tools"
type: pychon script
version: "1.0"

authors:
  - family-names: "Feng"
    given-names: "Linjing"
    email: "linjingfeng2021@gmail.com"

abstract: >-
  Python tools for fitting molecular-cloud column-density probability
  distribution functions (N-PDFs) using unbinned maximum-likelihood
  estimation and Markov Chain Monte Carlo sampling. The software supports
  lognormal, power-law, and combined lognormal-plus-power-law models.

keywords:
  - astronomy
  - molecular clouds
  - column density probability distribution function
  - maximum-likelihood estimation
  - Markov Chain Monte Carlo

license: MIT
